 ### Implementation for User Story 1
 
-- [ ] T014 [US1] Implement `plan_members(given_paths, archive_path) -> CreationPlan` in `src/tarx/create.py` — Pass 1, which writes nothing (FR-118). For each PATH in command-line order: build a `SourcePath` via `paths.validate_source_path` (T004) with `name = "/".join(components)`; `os.lstat` the path and refuse anything that is not a regular file or a directory; for a file emit one `PlannedMember(kind="file", size=st_size)`; for a directory emit the directory member first, then walk it with an **explicit LIFO stack** (never recursion — research R-106) using `os.scandir(follow_symlinks=False)`, taking each entry's kind from `DirEntry.is_dir(follow_symlinks=False)` / `is_file(follow_symlinks=False)` / `is_symlink()`, pushing entries sorted by name as Python `str` (code-point order) so they are visited ascending and each subdirectory's contents follow immediately after its own member (pre-order depth-first, FR-106, research R-107). Compute `file_count` as the number of `kind == "file"` members and `total_bytes` as the sum of their `size`. Docstring names FR-103, FR-104, FR-105, FR-106, FR-118, SR-103.
-- [ ] T015 [US1] Add member-name gating to `plan_members` in `src/tarx/create.py`: every computed member name is passed through the existing `paths.validate_member_name` — the very function `extract` uses — before Pass 2 begins, so FR-109's round-trip promise is an executed check rather than an argument (research R-112). A rejected name raises `TarxError`, exit 2. Depends on T014.
-- [ ] T016 [US1] Implement the header builder in `src/tarx/create.py` — a helper returning a `tarfile.TarInfo` constructed **field by field**, never via `TarFile.add()` or `TarFile.gettarinfo()` (research R-101, SR-108): `name` from `PlannedMember.name` with no trailing slash for directories; `type` `REGTYPE` or `DIRTYPE` only; `size` from `os.fstat` on the open descriptor for files and `0` for directories; `mode` `MEMBER_FILE_MODE` / `MEMBER_DIR_MODE`; `uid = gid = 0`; `uname = gname = ""`; `mtime = 0`; `linkname = ""`. No on-disk `st_mode`, `st_uid`, `st_gid`, or `st_mtime` value may reach any header field.
-- [ ] T017 [US1] Implement `write_archive(plan, target) -> None` in `src/tarx/create.py` — Pass 2. Create the output with `tempfile.mkstemp(dir=<ARCHIVE's own directory>, prefix=".tarx-", suffix=".tmp")`, which creates with `O_CREAT|O_EXCL` and mode `0o600` at creation and must never be followed by a `chmod` (SR-107, research R-104); the temporary must live in ARCHIVE's own directory so `os.rename` never crosses a filesystem boundary. Wrap the descriptor in `gzip.GzipFile(filename="", mode="wb", fileobj=raw, mtime=0)` when `target.compressed`, then in `tarfile.open(fileobj=..., mode="w:", format=tarfile.PAX_FORMAT)` — `PAX_FORMAT` named explicitly, never `DEFAULT_FORMAT` (research R-102, R-103). Stream each file member's contents in `COPY_CHUNK_BYTES` (64 KiB) chunks so no file is ever held whole in memory (SR-106), emit directory members with `addfile(tarinfo)` and no payload, then close every layer and `os.rename` the temporary onto `target.path` as the final act. The whole body sits in a `try/finally` that `os.unlink`s the temporary file on every path that does not reach a successful rename, so no partial archive and no leftover temporary can survive (FR-119). Depends on T016.
